    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0073","sequence":85,
      "meaning":"The Brahmin in Umā’s dream tells the mountain princess to go practice austerity, recognizing Nārada’s words as true; he adds that this counsel pleases her parents too, for austerity gives joy and destroys sorrow and fault. Through austerity’s power Brahmā creates the cosmos, Viṣṇu protects the whole world, Śambhu dissolves it, and Śeṣa bears the earth’s weight. All creation rests on austerity, so Bhavānī should go practice it with this understanding. Astonished by these words, her mother calls Himālaya and recounts the dream. After explaining herself to both parents in many ways, Umā joyfully departs for austerity. Her dear family, father and mother are so overwhelmed that words do not reach their mouths. The sage Vedaśirā then comes and counsels them all; hearing Pārvatī’s greatness, they receive understanding.",
