    {
      "entryId":"ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0075","sequence":87,
      "meaning":"The divine voice tells Bhavānī that no one has performed austerity like hers, though many steadfast and wise sages have lived. She must hold Brahmā’s boon-giving utterance in her heart as eternally true and pure. When her father comes to call her, she should abandon insistence and immediately return home. When the Seven Sages meet her, she may accept that as confirmation of the divine voice. Hearing fate’s proclamation from the sky, Girijā thrills bodily and rejoices. The poet has sung Umā’s lovely story and now turns to Śambhu’s beautiful course. From the moment Satī abandoned her body, detachment filled Śiva’s mind. He continually repeats Raghunāyaka’s name and listens everywhere to the hosts of Rāma’s virtues. Śiva—consciousness and bliss, abode of joy, beyond delusion, pride and desire—wanders the earth bearing in his heart Hari, delight of every world.",
